#!/bin/bash
# Start Dash and Python rotary encoder script in parallel with logging

# Go to Desktop
cd /home/pi/Desktop || exit 1

# Create logs directory if it doesn’t exist
mkdir -p logs

# Timestamps for log files
NOW=$(date +"%Y-%m-%d_%H-%M-%S")

# Start dash and log output
./dash > logs/dash_${NOW}.log 2>&1 &

# Start Python script and log output
python3 script.py > logs/script_${NOW}.log 2>&1 &

# Wait for both background processes
wait

🔑 What this does

Creates a logs/ folder on your Desktop.

Each boot/run creates new log files like:

logs/dash_2025-09-24_14-55-12.log
logs/script_2025-09-24_14-55-12.log


> file.log 2>&1 captures both stdout and stderr.

You can still monitor live logs via:

journalctl -u dash.service -f
